# User Service

Ghostty ships a systemd user unit, app-com.mitchellh.ghostty.service, that
starts a windowless Ghostty owning the com.mitchellh.ghostty dbus name. The
runit alternative is a user service managed by turnstile, installed in
/usr/share/examples/ghostty/.

To enable the service for your user:

	mkdir ~/.config/service/ghostty
	ln -s /usr/share/examples/ghostty/ghostty.run ~/.config/service/ghostty/run
	ln -s /usr/share/examples/ghostty/ghostty.check ~/.config/service/ghostty/check

$TURNSTILE_ENV_DIR needs WAYLAND_DISPLAY (or DISPLAY) and
DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS.

## Logging

Output goes to svlogtail under the turnstiled tag. To tag it as ghostty:

	mkdir ~/.config/service/ghostty/log
	ln -s /usr/bin/vlogger ~/.config/service/ghostty/log/run
